      en: "The Estadio Metropolitano Roberto Meléndez is a legendary football stadium in Barranquilla and the official home of the Colombian national football team. Known as the 'House of the National Team', it is famous for its intense and passionate atmosphere, particularly during World Cup qualifying matches. The stadium's design features a distinctive shell-like roof and a capacity of nearly 47,000 spectators, making it one of the largest in the country. Inaugurated in 1986, it was named after Roberto Meléndez, a beloved local football hero who was Colombia's first great striker. The stadium is also the home of the local club Junior de Barranquilla, one of the most successful teams in the Colombian league. Its location in the heat of the Caribbean coast is considered a strategic advantage for the national team, as visiting opponents often struggle with the humidity. It remains a temple of Colombian football and a symbol of the nation's sporting pride."
