      en: "The Estadio Nemesio Camacho El Campín is the historical and emotional heart of football in Bogotá. Inaugurated in 1938, it is the city's most important sports stadium and has been the stage for many of the most memorable moments in Colombian football history. It is the home ground for the capital's two most successful clubs, Millonarios and Santa Fe, who share a fierce rivalry known as the 'Clásico Capitalino'. The stadium's name honors Nemesio Camacho, a prominent politician whose family donated the land for its construction. With a capacity for nearly 40,000 fans, El Campín is famous for its electric atmosphere, especially during finals and international matches. Over the years, it has undergone several renovations to modernize its facilities while maintaining its historic character. Beyond sports, the stadium has also hosted legendary concerts by international artists, making it a central venue for the city's cultural life. It remains a sacred site for football fans in Bogotá and a symbol of the city's sporting passion."
