      en: "The 'Ventana al Mundo' (Window to the World) is a vibrant and modern monument that has quickly become a new icon for the city of Barranquilla. Inaugurated in 2018, this giant structure stands 45 meters tall and is composed of over 2,000 square meters of colorful laminated glass in shades of blue, green, and red. Its unique design, featuring two leaning pillars that meet at the top to form a frame, symbolizes the industrial power of Barranquilla and its historical role as Colombia's gateway to the world. The monument is located in a large public park that includes interactive fountains and a timeline of the city's most important historical events. At night, it is spectacular, with internal lights that make the glass pillars glow with intense colors. It was donated to the city by the local company Tecnoglass and has become a popular destination for both locals and tourists. The 'Window to the World' represents the optimism and the modern transformation of Barranquilla as a leading Caribbean metropolis."
